[Applause]  just days ago millions of people took to  the streets across the world demanding  more action on climate change now  leaders gather at the United Nations in  New York where Luis Alfonso de Alba is  in charge of the climate summit his  message the Paris climate agreement is  no longer enough the biggest problem we  have is that we need to increase the  targets if we fulfill the commitments  that were made in Paris in 2015 we will  still be very much below what what is  needed the latest reports of the  scientific community tell us that we  need to double and in some cases to  triple what we have committed in Paris  but there's a problem with this ambition  far from doing more America one of the  world's biggest polluters is pulling out  of the Paris Accord can the world really  make the progress it needs to  while Donald Trump is in office no one  is telling us that they are going to  wait for the orders to move before they  do and the more the majority is moving  on this is not a problem for 2030 2050  but actions need to take place today  former United Nations secretary-general  ban ki-moon is optimistic big looters  like China and the UK are expected to  make new commitments and eventually he  thinks the US will fall into line I'm  sure that United said we'll have to  return to this because climate change  does not respect the national borders  the United State is just one of the  desert planet Earth the nature does not  negotiate with the human society but  there are other geopolitical headwinds  creating challenges the countries  gathering here at the United Nations in  New York for the climate summit have  been told that if they even want a  speaking slot they have to bring  enhanced commitments and  concrete plans there's a lot going on in  the world right now that might make that  more difficult like escalating trade  issues between China in the US tensions  with Iran and BRICS it the kind of  things that make countries focus on  their own needs and collective action on  anything much harder to achieve with the  eyes of the world on the United Nations  the pressure to do more on climate  change is building along with the cost  of doing nothing Hannah Thomas Peter Sky  News in New York

